2026-02-11 01:03:49,884 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Is IRR?

IRR, or internal rate of return, is a metric used in financial analysis to estimate the profitability of potential investments. IRR is a discount rate that makes the net present value (NPV) of all cash flows equal to zero in a discounted cash flow analysis.

In simple terms, IRR indicates the annualized rate of return a project or investment is expected to generate. A higher IRR signals a more attractive investment. No matter what type of project or investment you’re analyzing (a new factory, a real estate deal, a tech startup, etc.), the IRR formula is the same. The consistency of calculating the IRR across all opportunities makes it an excellent metric for investors to use in ranking and comparing projects. is relevant
